#X obj 667 8 expand_env;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 261 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object substitutes environment variables in incoming
symbols \, lists or messages. Variables are written as %NAME% and are
replaced with the corresponding value from the environment \, for example
%HOME% is replaced by the user's home directory under UNIX. Variables
can appear anywhere inside a symbol \, not just at the beginning: for
example \, "user:%USER%" becomes "user:alice".;
#X text 240 199 Some special variables are defined by the library:
%DOC% — path to the PureData documentation directory \, %CEAMMC% —
path to the ceammc library directory.;
#X text 240 254 By default only the arguments (list elements or symbol
parts) are expanded \, not the message selector. With the @any flag
\, substitution is also performed in the message selector.;
